# Codex Collab Settings Example

Copy this file to `.claude/codex-collab.local.md` and customize for your project.

---
model: o4-mini
sandbox: read-only
language: en               # Response language for Codex: en | ja | etc.
                           # When set to non-English, adds language directive to all prompts.
                           # For ja: "日本語で回答してください。途中の説明や思考プロセスも日本語で..."
                           # This ensures both final output and thinking process are in the target language.

# Timeout settings
codex:
  wait_timeout: 180        # seconds (default: 180, max: 600)

# Launch mode settings (how Codex is launched)
launch:
  mode: auto               # auto | wt | tmux | inline
                           # auto: tmuxセッション内→tmux, それ以外→wt→inline
                           # tmux: 現在のペインを水平分割し右側で実行
                           # inline: 現在のターミナルで実行（ブロッキング）
  # tmux_socket: /absolute/path/to/collab.sock
                           # tmux ソケットの絶対パス（オプション）
                           # 設定すると環境変数 CODEX_TMUX_SOCKET として使用される
                           # 未設定の場合は $TMUX から自動検出

# Planning exchange settings (Codex plans → Claude questions → Codex refines)
exchange:
  enabled: true              # Global kill-switch for planning exchanges
  max_iterations: 3
  user_confirm: on_important # never | always | on_important
  history_mode: summarize    # full | summarize

# Review iteration settings (Codex reviews → Claude fixes → Codex re-reviews)
review:
  enabled: true              # Enable/disable review iterations
  max_iterations: 5          # Can be higher than exchange (goal is clear, diff is small)
  max_verdict_retries: 3     # Retries when verdict is missing/unclear from Codex
  user_confirm: never        # Auto-iterate for reviews
---

## Project-specific Instructions

Add any project-specific context here that should be included when collaborating with Codex.

### Example Instructions

- This project uses TypeScript with strict mode
- Follow the existing code style in `src/`
- All new files should include unit tests in `__tests__/`
- Use functional components for React code
